  "implementation_instructions": [
    "Run this task prepare_minimal_plan.py with a fresh --output path; it verifies metadata/source pins and writes two comparison specifications, without reading requests/weights, importing models or launching.",
    "For later engineering, use the existing fixed-stage qualify.py run/collect loop and bev_native_dev_probe.CaptureModel/persist_operand plus the exact ordinal runtime collect_one function. Add an ordinal entry arm in a separate fresh diagnostic wrapper, not in frozen scientific requests or the production 140-row runtime.",
    "Reuse the existing three native_long_dev_20261103_v2/inference/requests.jsonl rows unchanged for each model. collect_one needs only rendered_prompt and input_ids; it can consume those already prepared native rows directly. Do not call ordinal runtime run/verify (140-row contract and weight rehash) or probe.collect_one (4096 cap). Do not call old qualify.run unchanged: that would repeat all reference/repeat/adapter forwards.",
    "Load each Base once using the ordinal pinned load_model. Call the unchanged ordinal collect_one once for each of the three frozen rows; persist full arrays using the existing exclusive-create persistence helper. Model eval FP32, conv/matmul HF32 false, batch1, no truncation, logits_to_keep=1, inference_mode, no cache/attention/precision overrides.",
    "Reuse each accepted reference/reference_repeat/adapter operand as historical comparison input, after receipt/custody validation in the later authorized comparison. Compare all full-vector coordinates to the new ordinal vector, allowing only singleton batch-axis normalization; input IDs and masks must be equal in dtype/shape/value. No shared-output right-hand operand; one new invocation per row. Tolerance remains zero. A mismatch stops reuse; never loosen thresholds.",
    "Bind new collector/source/runtime and exact model/image/environment/call-shape identities plus old origins in the resulting comparison receipt. Record actual new container/environment/driver-library mounts separately; image equality alone cannot discharge host-mounted runtime differences. Do not claim source-identical model code across changed external mounts.",
    "CPU-only postprocessing may project digit15..19 and16..20 and full-vocab mass using the frozen ordinal scorer; existing six-label score projection is not itself the five-label ordinal denominator. Reuse admitted B1/scientific arithmetic without changing ties or scientific metrics. No label-specific NPU forwards.",
    "Before using this scope in host approval, implement an explicit new evidence schema that binds the arithmetic tuple, this amendment, and an allowlisted mapping to all eight exact config/request receipts. Keep exact config/command/resource approval separate. Old approval() is unchanged and still rejects this scope document as numerical PASS.",
